From: Maciej Krüger <mkg20001@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: uc: add missing string.h include

client.c and server.c use memset/strcpy without including string.h.
GCC 14 turns implicit function declarations into hard errors, so uc
no longer builds.

diff --git a/utils/uc/patches/0001-add-missing-string.h-include.patch b/utils/uc/patches/0001-add-missing-string.h-include.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/utils/uc/patches/0001-add-missing-string.h-include.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+--- a/client.c
++++ b/client.c
+@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
+ #include <sys/socket.h>
+ #include <sys/un.h>
+ #include <unistd.h>
++#include <string.h>
+ #include <sys/epoll.h>
+ #include <errno.h>
+ #include <stdarg.h>
+--- a/server.c
++++ b/server.c
+@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
+ #include <sys/socket.h>
+ #include <sys/un.h>
+ #include <unistd.h>
++#include <string.h>
+
+ #define SOCK_FILE "server.sock"
+
